From: Jesse Osiecki <jesse@jjo.ninja>
Subject: [PATCH] lockscreen: start authenticating again when the screen wakes

The non-interactive authenticators (fingerprint, or a face module in the
kde-fingerprint PAM slot) run one PAM conversation per
startAuthenticating() call. The mobile lock screen only calls it when it
is created, when a password is tried and after a failed try, so after the
screen turns off (idle, power button, suspend) the reader stays idle until
the user types something. Re-arm it when DPMS turns the screen back on,
which is exactly when the user is looking at the device again.

Signed-off-by: Jesse Osiecki <jesse@jjo.ninja>
---
 shell/contents/lockscreen/LockScreen.qml | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/shell/contents/lockscreen/LockScreen.qml b/shell/contents/lockscreen/LockScreen.qml
--- a/shell/contents/lockscreen/LockScreen.qml
+++ b/shell/contents/lockscreen/LockScreen.qml
@@ -95,6 +95,14 @@
                 lockScreenState.resetPassword();
             }
         }
+
+        // Non-interactive authenticators (fingerprint, face) stop when their
+        // PAM conversation ends; arm them again when the screen wakes up.
+        onDpmsTurnedOn: (screen) => {
+            if (screen.name === Screen.name) {
+                authenticator.startAuthenticating();
+            }
+        }
     }
 
     // Container for lockscreen contents
